From 94a9371de7de72d4fd6f7375afa1c2c5271f434b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:51:23 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 252/405] Unified: the bar next to a pick follows a table of
 rules, with a number to type
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

What the bar offers is now data (ContextRules.py, as in chapter 6.4 of the
design): the kind of the picked things (sketch, flat / round / other face,
straight / circle / other edge, several edges, point, part, two picks on
two parts, two parts, mesh, lines of an opened 2D drawing, and in technical
drawings a circle, a line, two lines, a view, a page) gives the tools from
left to right. Tools of modules not loaded yet are offered too and load
their module when used (meshes: check and fix, make a solid).

The first tool that takes a number has a field next to it (extrude 10 mm,
fillet 2 mm …): type the number and Enter, and the tool is done without
its panel (the last number is remembered); its button opens the panel for
everything else. Typing digits in the view goes into the field. Last but
one is "Ask AI", last "…": every tool that works with the pick. New
commands pick the other edges in the same direction and the other circles
of the same size. The bar also appears for picks on a drawing page.
Tested without the GUI: FreeCADCmd -t TestContextRules.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
